# GW1 Live Trade Prices — environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env and fill in what you need; `npm start`/`npm run backfill` pick
# it up automatically via Node's built-in --env-file-if-exists (no dotenv
# dependency). Running `node bin/gw1-prices.mjs` directly does NOT read this
# file unless you add the same flag yourself — everything here also works as
# a plain shell export, a systemd Environment= line, or a compose
# environment: entry, which is what the deploy docs use.
#
# This list is exhaustive: these are the only environment variables the app
# reads. CLI flags (see `node bin/gw1-prices.mjs --help`) cover the same
# ground and win if both are set. A variable already set in your shell also
# wins over this file — Node's --env-file never overrides an existing value,
# it only fills in what's missing — so `export PORT=...` left over in a
# terminal will silently shadow whatever you put here.

# Port and bind address. 127.0.0.1 (default) is loopback-only; 0.0.0.0
# exposes it beyond this machine — see the README's Authentication section
# and deploy/DEPLOY.md before doing that.
PORT=8787
HOST=127.0.0.1

# HTTP Basic Auth, off by default. Set both or neither — the process refuses
# to start with only one. Basic Auth is base64 in transit, not encryption;
# see the README before relying on it alone over the open internet.
# AUTH_USER=alan
# AUTH_PASS=something-long-and-unique

# Folder holding a GWToolbox inventory export (or a synced copy of one) to
# watch and re-import automatically on change. Same as --watch.
# WATCH_DIR=/path/to/inventories

# Pull ~90 days of NPC trader history on startup. Same as --backfill. Do not
# combine with a "no network calls" setting — there isn't one via env var;
# use --no-poll on the CLI directly if you want that.
# BACKFILL=true
